<description>&lt;p&gt;President de la Espriella opened a Colombian embassy in Jerusalem, drawing condemnation from Pakistan and other Muslim states, and announced a cultural counterrevolution that includes removing more than thirty artworks from the National Museum. Opposition groups protested his budget cuts that threaten the peace tribunal and searches for the disappeared, while the peace tribunal charged former FARC members with anti-Indigenous crimes. An acid-attack survivor cancelled a planned euthanasia after a public appeal, and a preacher was killed by members of a criminal group in Cartagena. 225 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE1TTTkyVGppeko1WEFvMmEzamUxWU9rVzBaOEh6MklzRUhjRUVaWkJidHEweHFXTDcyT2dERWt4ZDV6bG9hSVdvVWtrTXpLcVRqZjhBVUVNZ2hqdkct?oc=5&quot;&gt;International Crisis Group&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxOMHdqckFXeU5Pc0hXUmNvR0Q2LUx1Y29Mdkh0V2VpbUh0Y3MyR2NDb2t3UTRkVkoycU5yUTBQckllc1VGeHhyeFhsOWFxaVowd2FvakVHS3V1WFFIQjR5TUxISTVfRXQ2M29vN1F0ME1qektaZFFBZVVlN2FKQUdHMFdEY2xyWHdBUXo5UjV6cjlwZmpmMk9VV3Q5c0oyT192MV92UU5n?oc=5&quot;&gt;ColombiaOne.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxObmpBLTFZaUVOTG1acHIzQzBLUXBjb180QkI0SWg4cWE1bmhjOTBHWkxHQnR5aXo0UjFhR3VvM2kwSnR0TDdEUDBPSEpmOGU3emQ4QWh2MUJMSmxFS1VvdDNRUHp0eDR4RjI3MGlKZnZJdHlRR3BsWS1mbmYzdzJmeXczOUwyMnJXN1RSUWpTUzZVV1FlOWQ4V19QMEoteVBIUl9fQTBGSVlkY3dIN1JsM2d5Ylo?oc=5&quot;&gt;Latin America Reports&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxNOW5Tc1RTQTJHeXJmTTRZZ2JrVllhcDAzb1NybGNhQTlDRFpsby1la08za